# Relations between factions and enemy exclusion (DESIGN.md §9.4): factions regard each
# other from -100 to 100, and two are in conflict when either regards the other at or below
# -50. A member of one can't join the other.
load content/sample
relations city_watch
# The Watch and the mercenaries are rivals, but not in conflict.
relations free_company
# A thief joins the Lantern Guild, and the Watch turns them away on both counts.
act player steal --scale 4
join player lantern_guild
can-join player city_watch --explain
# A truce lifts the enemy bar; distance still keeps the player out.
relate city_watch lantern_guild --by 40
assert can-join player city_watch == no: 90.35 from The City Watch, tolerance is 40.00
# A one-way grudge is enough for conflict.
relate city_watch free_company -60 --one-way
relations free_company
# A war between two of the player's own factions opens a conflict for the game to settle
# (see wars.scenario).
join player free_company
relate lantern_guild free_company -60
journal
